# Agent DSL

This Livebook uses the Jido Agent DSL to declare a data schema, routes, route
defaults, and generated interfaces. The declaration produces a reusable Agent
definition.

## Install Jido

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)}
])
```

## Define A Named Action

```elixir
defmodule AgentDSL.Rename do
  use Jido.Action,
    name: "agent_dsl_rename",
    schema: Zoi.object(%{name: Zoi.string()})

  @impl Jido.Action
  def run(%{name: name}, %{agent_state: state}) do
    {:ok, %{state | name: String.trim(name)}}
  end
end
```

## Declare The Agent

```elixir
defmodule AgentDSL.Profile do
  use Jido.Agent,
    name: "agent_dsl_profile",
    description: "Owns one display profile"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{
             name: Zoi.string() |> Zoi.default("Anonymous"),
             revision: Zoi.integer() |> Zoi.min(0) |> Zoi.default(0)
           })

    metadata %{domain: "profiles"}
  end

  routes do
    signal_source "/guides/agent-dsl"

    route "profile.rename", AgentDSL.Rename do
      defaults %{name: "Anonymous"}
      define :rename, args: [{:optional, :name}]
    end
  end
end
```

Each field has one source. Jido rejects a field that appears in both the
`use Jido.Agent` options and its DSL block.

The DSL is declarative. It describes the Agent and generates its definition and
interfaces. It does not start an Agent Server.

## Inspect Generated Data

```elixir
definition = AgentDSL.Profile.agent()

%{
  name: AgentDSL.Profile.name(),
  description: AgentDSL.Profile.description(),
  metadata: AgentDSL.Profile.metadata(),
  routes: AgentDSL.Profile.routes(),
  definition?: Jido.Agent.definition?(definition)
}
```

## Instantiate And Use The Generated Interface

```elixir
agent = AgentDSL.Profile.new!(id: "profile-1")
{:ok, signal} = AgentDSL.Profile.rename_signal(" Ada ")
{:ok, candidate, []} = AgentDSL.Profile.cmd(agent, signal)

candidate.state.name
```

The result is `"Ada"`.

## Use A Route Default

```elixir
{:ok, signal} = AgentDSL.Profile.rename_signal()
{:ok, candidate, []} = AgentDSL.Profile.cmd(agent, signal)

candidate.state.name
```

The result is `"Anonymous"`. Signal values replace route defaults when both
provide the same key.

